> ```

Yes, the [documentation](https://quarkus.io/guides/lifecycle#startup_annotation) is pretty clear that _"The `@Startup` annotation can be also declared on a non-static non-producer no-args method"_.

If you need to initialize the beans backed by the producer methods during startup you would need something like this instead:
```java
void onStart(@Observes StartupEvent event, KafkaStreams ks, KafkaStreamsTopologyManager kstm) {}
```
The injection points trigger the producers.
